<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB leaves discount rate unchanged after meeting.</title>
<headline>SNB leaves discount rate unchanged after meeting.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank (SNB) said that it left its discount rate unchanged at one percent after a regular meeting of its three-man board.</p>
<p>&quot;No change,&quot; a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The discount rate has been at one percent since it was lowered from 1.50 percent on September 26.</p>
<p>Markets had not expected any change in the discount rate at today's meeting. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
